<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan grains/oilseeds tender results - December.</title>
<headline>Taiwan grains/oilseeds tender results - December.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan interests bought in December a total of 28,000 tonnes of U.S. soybeans, 32,000 tonnes of U.S. corn and 72,000 tonnes U.S. wheat at tenders.</p>
<p>December soybean/corn tender results:</p>
<p>(Prices based on US$ per tonne)</p>
<p> Dec Buyer     Tonne  Type  Delivery	Seller Price/Freight</p>
<p>  6  T. Sugar  18,000 soy   Jan 10-25     Contine $284.36/FOB</p>
<p>		   12,000 corn			     $131.46/FOB</p>
<p> 24  T. Sugar  10,000 soy   Feb 15-31     Contine $.12694/CNF</p>
<p>		   20,000 corn			     $.11724/CNF</p>
<p>Delivery periods for soybean and corn shipments are stated for the U.S. Gulf of Mexico. Shipments originating from the Pacific Northwest are 15 days after those from the Gulf.</p>
<p>December wheat tender results:</p>
<p>(Prices based on US$ per tonne)</p>
<p> Nov Buyer     Tonne  Type  Delivery	Seller  Price/Freight</p>
<p>     Flour			Dec 15-Jan  5		     $19.50</p>
<p>     Mill	16,600 DNS		    CGI     $196.67</p>
<p>     Assoc     10,700 HRW		    Mitsui  $191.70</p>
<p>		    6,700  WW		    Mitsui  $155.30</p>
<p>     Flour			Dec 30-Jan 20		     $19.40</p>
<p>     Mill	22,400 DNS		    Mitshui $195.30</p>
<p>     Assoc	9,400 HRW		    CGI     $190.87</p>
<p>		    6,200  WW		    Cargill $155.25</p>
<p>December wheat tenders comprised dark northern spring (DNS), hard red winter (HRW), white wheat (WW) and soft wheat (SW).</p>
<p>Wheat shipments all are slated for delivery from the Pacific Northwest.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
